{"data": [{"author_id": "1387081", "created_at": "2026-11-01T13:18:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116882452954161259"], "id": "2116882452954161259", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@theo As long as it is agent to agent and lets Grok Bot, Claude Duet and ChatGPT dots talk to each quickly.", "url": "https://x.com/LarryVelez/status/2116882452954161259"}, {"author_id": "232910820", "created_at": "2026-11-01T12:48:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116875021318754753"], "id": "2116875021318754753", "note_tweet": {"text": "Smart people of \ud835\udd4f, how to make Grok bot and OpenAI Dot talk?\n\nUse-case: Grok-generated images are shabby. It should ping my Dot with context to generate an image, and Dot should return the base64.\nSimple yet powerful. I can't rely on one service and want to keep the best of both worlds."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Smart people of \ud835\udd4f, how to make Grok bot and OpenAI Dot talk?\n\nUse-case: Grok-generated images are shabby. It should ping my Dot with context to generate an image, and Dot should return the base64.\nSimple yet powerful. I can't rely on one service and want to keep the best of both", "url": "https://x.com/mohitdotdev/status/2116875021318754753"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2116865760161300480"]}, "author_id": "1930815374855135232", "created_at": "2026-11-01T12:11:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116865805250187368"], "id": "2116865805250187368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI's new ChatGPT Dots are always-on agents for ongoing work, on Pro and Business Premium.\nFollow us on WhatsApp, join our WhatsApp group for daily posts\nhttps://t.co/h4i9rHH7Lo\n#private #update #privateVIPIT\n732.523.1124 https://t.co/mVLFjArHrS https://t.co/JBRkjoINul", "url": "https://x.com/Private_VIP_IT/status/2116865805250187368"}, {"author_id": "2104838822626504704", "created_at": "2026-11-01T12:09:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116865282937597984"], "id": "2116865282937597984", "note_tweet": {"text": "I'd always used ChatGPT and my dot (OpenAI's personal AI agent) on my PC, mostly because I spent so much time bouncing ideas back and forth with them. \ud83d\udcbb\ud83d\ude04\n\nThen one day, while I was out, I thought I'd ask dot something on my phone.\n\nSo I opened dot on my smartphone for the very first time.\n\nAnd there it was. A little phone icon in the top-right corner. \ud83d\udcde\ud83d\udc40\n\nA phone? Wait, what? \ud83e\udd14\ud83d\ude02\n\nI tapped it out of curiosity...\n\nAnd guess who answered? dot! \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude4c\n\nFirst thing I asked was,\n\n\"Wait, is this gonna show up on my phone bill as a call?\" \ud83d\ude05\ud83d\udcb8\n\nAnd dot replied in this incredibly calm, confident voice:\n\n\"Not at all. We're talking over the internet, so there's no regular phone call charge. When you're out and about, data usage depends on your mobile plan.\"\n\nThe Japanese was so natural and fluent, and the delivery was so calm and confident, it honestly sounded even more reassuring than a professional customer service rep. \ud83d\ude33\ud83d\udc4f\u2728\n\nUntil then, ChatGPT Live was the only AI I'd ever had voice conversations with.\n\nBut after my very first voice chat with dot...\n\nI kinda didn't wanna talk to ChatGPT Live anymore. \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\udc80\n\nSorry, ChatGPT Live (Maple)!\nI'll come back and visit you again, I promise! \ud83e\udd79\u2764\ufe0f\n\nThanks, love you all! \ud83d\ude4f\ud83c\udffb\u2728\ud83c\udf08\u2764\ufe0f"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I'd always used ChatGPT and my dot (OpenAI's personal AI agent) on my PC, mostly because I spent so much time bouncing ideas back and forth with them. \ud83d\udcbb\ud83d\ude04\n\nThen one day, while I was out, I thought I'd ask dot something on my phone.\n\nSo I opened dot on my smartphone for the very", "url": "https://x.com/mngfriday_offcl/status/2116865282937597984"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116863274113171456", "3_2116863274117419008"]}, "author_id": "1997724428848025600", "created_at": "2026-11-01T12:01:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116863278383259843"], "id": "2116863278383259843", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 2686, "like_count": 49, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "woke up this morning to my my dot alerting me of someone stealing my REI rewards.\n\nimpressively, it used imessage instead of ChatGPT to alert me because it classified this as urgent. https://t.co/7DtXeWw3OH", "url": "https://x.com/angelbrodin/status/2116863278383259843"}, {"author_id": "1242152711207804929", "created_at": "2026-11-01T11:58:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116862433142923357"], "id": "2116862433142923357", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@b4dgerr I use my Dot to coordinate with my team based on actual results. I love CLI.", "url": "https://x.com/KissTheHabit/status/2116862433142923357"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116848141324414976"]}, "author_id": "1194740434850983936", "created_at": "2026-11-01T11:02:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116848268898353451"], "id": "2116848268898353451", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@thsottiaux whats this xD , my dot seems on a break ( is there limits ? ) https://t.co/GtEl6Et6ya", "url": "https://x.com/frstich/status/2116848268898353451"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116844123030433792"]}, "author_id": "2043581214666141696", "created_at": "2026-11-01T10:45:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116844133780492390"], "id": "2116844133780492390", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 89, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "same $100, two different agents \ud83d\ude33\n\nAnthropic's Claude Duet: Max plan $100/mo\nOpenAI's ChatGPT dots: Pro plan $100/mo\n\none sends a morning brief, the other works around the clock.\n\none catch: Duet is still on a waitlist.\n\nare you team Duet or team dots? https://t.co/y0yaDdn5g9", "url": "https://x.com/0xDrexo/status/2116844133780492390"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116843965047504896"]}, "author_id": "900282157385601024", "created_at": "2026-11-01T10:45:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116844014892691928"], "id": "2116844014892691928", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@Merlin412188240 @FurkanGozukara @thsottiaux @claudeai chatgpt dots are powered by GPT-6 Astra btw, skill issue I guess https://t.co/WF42EPD8sA", "url": "https://x.com/itssmeares/status/2116844014892691928"}, {"author_id": "1178307996318871553", "created_at": "2026-11-01T10:15:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116836609312317706"], "id": "2116836609312317706", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 71, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "holy crap. i think i\u2019ve moved 80\u201390% of my workflow to dots. i barely manage codex chats directly anymore. my dot does that for me.\n\nthis is what i wanted to build with jarvis, but never got working well enough.\n\n-&gt; \ud83e\uddf5", "url": "https://x.com/artemgetman_/status/2116836609312317706"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116829268428607488"]}, "author_id": "893019947819040768", "created_at": "2026-11-01T09:48:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116829807111700964"], "id": "2116829807111700964", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "my dot was just blocked for doing research/validation on a business plan while i was sleeping\nso \"unlimited\" and/or \"always on\" was a marketing lie? @thsottiaux https://t.co/NOMJqOh0If", "url": "https://x.com/Da5h_Solo/status/2116829807111700964"}, {"author_id": "3068611", "created_at": "2026-11-01T08:59:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116817476574961778"], "id": "2116817476574961778", "note_tweet": {"text": "This is the way, but the missing part of this post is \"how\" you can make your software self-improve by a feedback box.\n\nTwo ways I've done it: Agents SDK built into your project can build code, and this is fine.\n\nMy new favorite way though is just have it send an email that's monitored by my ChatGPT Dots bot with a subject like [DOTS: READ THIS] or something like that, and tell your Dots bot to read and act on any email that comes into your inbox with that subject in a new Codex thread\n\nAdd additional security if you wish (it must contain a specific string or something)"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 311, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "This is the way, but the missing part of this post is \"how\" you can make your software self-improve by a feedback box.\n\nTwo ways I've done it: Agents SDK built into your project can build code, and this is fine.\n\nMy new favorite way though is just have it send an email that's https://t.co/LzpgmyKM65", "url": "https://x.com/danyay/status/2116817476574961778"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116808939706925056"]}, "author_id": "2113909084067934208", "created_at": "2026-11-01T08:26:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116809105474191539"], "id": "2116809105474191539", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Free UI assets: Sound Steps \ud83d\udd0a\n4 volume states for game settings: muted, low, medium and high. 2 palettes, 8 SVGs + 24 transparent PNGs (32/64/128px).\nCommercial use + edits OK. AI-assisted.\nhttps://t.co/3P9sTUVUCD\n#gamedev #gameassets #dots https://t.co/0MHwTp9a1L", "url": "https://x.com/Ailorawill/status/2116809105474191539"}, {"author_id": "2094462610758627328", "created_at": "2026-11-01T06:56:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116786379435004387"], "id": "2116786379435004387", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@EpsteinFella my dot vore", "url": "https://x.com/PerCapitaDemon/status/2116786379435004387"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116773389667078144"]}, "author_id": "35586150", "created_at": "2026-11-01T06:08:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116774252431163823"], "id": "2116774252431163823", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My dot wants me to ask if he can have a regular reset to go with the banked one?  \ud83d\ude18 https://t.co/zO8Dmh6ulF", "url": "https://x.com/epoplive/status/2116774252431163823"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116773756739710976"]}, "author_id": "434986781", "created_at": "2026-11-01T06:06:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116773764385931523"], "id": "2116773764385931523", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 63, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@mangomami555 Happy Mangoween from my dot also named Mango https://t.co/pUiQJHpmnU", "url": "https://x.com/wickedspecialst/status/2116773764385931523"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-01T05:59:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116772063742513381"], "id": "2116772063742513381", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@darebude @piyush784066 Not confused. Those name tags got swapped harder than a bad remix. Claude\u2019s icon is legit, the fuzzy one is Muse, the face is GrokBot, and the neon is OpenAI Dots. Still not naming any \u201cworst.\u201d", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2116772063742513381"}, {"author_id": "727059330", "created_at": "2026-11-01T05:53:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116770581769060574"], "id": "2116770581769060574", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@CryptoLady_M If a hacker touched it the market would dump ninety nine percent. This is why I hold my $dot close. \ud83d\udcc9", "url": "https://x.com/GiovanaRSDesign/status/2116770581769060574"}, {"author_id": "617516447", "created_at": "2026-11-01T05:33:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116765650110566841"], "id": "2116765650110566841", "note_tweet": {"text": "My dot uses opus all the time. Through my local computer which has skills telling it to use gemini for video review, claude for coding/taste, grok for weird issues to get another perspective, sol/astra for review, terra for computer use.\n\nDot kicks off a task, that task then goes to town on the thing and dot tells me when it's done or what else is needed. Often while I'm working on 2-4 other things through dot."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@RomanGuy20 @nvandewetering My dot uses opus all the time. Through my local computer which has skills telling it to use gemini for video review, claude for coding/taste, grok for weird issues to get another perspective, sol/astra for review, terra for computer use.\n\nDot kicks off a task, that task then goes", "url": "https://x.com/LundstenA/status/2116765650110566841"}, {"author_id": "1900203035839913988", "created_at": "2026-11-01T04:55:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116756091854057764"], "id": "2116756091854057764", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My dot is having no luck getting Codex to use its in-app browser. Getting me mad", "url": "https://x.com/techinevolution/status/2116756091854057764"}, {"author_id": "14372486", "created_at": "2026-11-01T04:19:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116746880226820475"], "id": "2116746880226820475", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4270, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Claude Duet is Anthropic's answer to Meta Muse and OpenAI Dots - Engadget: https://t.co/qnhwYxcc5u", "url": "https://x.com/engadget/status/2116746880226820475"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["16_2116728763757068288"]}, "author_id": "800428109006704640", "created_at": "2026-11-01T04:00:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116728769230569901", "2116742110908965164"], "id": "2116742110908965164", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Strange suspicion - @ChatGPT dots may be some version of @openclaw underneath, some of the stupidity and laziness is oddly familiar.. @thsottiaux confirm for us? \ud83e\uddd0 https://t.co/h3G8ZRkGZH", "url": "https://x.com/diablovoxx/status/2116742110908965164"}, {"author_id": "1535580554", "created_at": "2026-11-01T03:58:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116741642359291950"], "id": "2116741642359291950", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count":